The whole process of a player (as opposed to a character) getting skilled at 
Nethack is to learn from game to game. Granted, this learning doesn't 
usually consist of knowing specifics from an earlier game, but if you 
imagine each adventurer to be wholly ignorant of the dungeon, and play 
accordingly, you'll never get anywhere.

I'd say if you're the type of player who plays with open spoilers all the 
time, then by all means use your old notes; if not, then rely on your 
memory. But specifics in notes won't help anyway, if what is meant is that 
crystal wands = wands of death, etc. The forms will be all rearranged.

Which leads to an interesting possibility: what if bones files recorded not 
what actual items an adventurer possessed, but their form? The bones pile 
wouldn't recall wands of death, but rather crystal wands, which in the new 
game might be secret door detection. Of course, bones pile items would have 
wierd distributions, but it's an interesting thought to ponder.
